.\" Title: vrunner
.\" Author: vrunner contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrunner.1

.TH VRUNNER 1 "2025" "vrunner" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrunner \- virtual terminal runner and process orchestrator with web control plane

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrunner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]]

.B vrunner
\fBlist\fR

.B vrunner
\fBstop\fR \fIPID\fR

.B vrunner
\fBcert\fR \fBgenerate\fR \fINAME\fR

.B vrunner
\fBcert\fR \fBlist\fR

.B vrunner
\fBcert\fR \fBshow\fR \fINAME\fR

.B vrunner
\fBcert\fR \fBremove\fR \fINAME\fR

.B vrunner
\fBspawn\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]

.B vrunner
\fBfreeze\fR \fIPID\fR

.B vrunner
\fBthaw\fR \fIPID\fR

.B vrunner
\fBlist\-vrunner\fR

.B vrunner
\fBlist\-commands\fR

.B vrunner
\fBstop\-command\fR \fITARGET\fR

.B vrunner
\fBresize\fR \fITARGET\fR [\fB\-\-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-cols\fR \fIN\fR]

.B vrunner
\fBpurge\fR [\fITARGET\fR]

.B vrunner
\fBconfig-check\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBvrunner\fR executes commands inside virtual TTYs (VTTYs), exposes their output through a web API, and provides a built-in administrative interface for remote control. By default, it runs silently with no terminal output, making it ideal for background development servers, CI pipelines, or headless environments.

Commands are run inside pseudo-terminals, giving child processes full terminal capabilities including ANSI colors, cursor movement, and interactive keyboard input. Once running, commands can be monitored and controlled from the CLI, the web admin dashboard, or the HTTP API.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS General Options

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Path to a configuration file. Supported formats: YAML (\fB.yaml\fR/\fB.yml\fR), TOML (\fB.toml\fR), JSON (\fB.json\fR). Overrides global and local config files.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SS Server Options

.TP
.B \-\-bind \fIADDR\fR
Server bind address (default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR). Use \fB0.0.0.0\fR to accept remote connections.

.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Server TCP port (default: \fB9090\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-remote
Convenience flag that binds to \fB0.0.0.0\fR and enables bearer token authentication. Equivalent to \fB\-\-bind 0.0.0.0 \-\-auth\fR.

.SS Security Options

.TP
.B \-\-auth
Require bearer token authentication for all API requests.

.TP
.B \-\-token\-file \fIFILE\fR
Path to the bearer token file (default: \fB~/.config/vrunner/token\fR). If the file does not exist when auth is required, a cryptographically random 256-bit token is generated and saved.

.SS TLS Options

.TP
.B \-\-tls
Enable TLS (HTTPS) with self-signed certificates. Certificates are auto-generated on first use and saved to \fB~/.config/vrunner/\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-cert\-file \fIFILE\fR
Path to a custom PEM-encoded TLS certificate file.

.TP
.B \-\-key\-file \fIFILE\fR
Path to a custom PEM-encoded TLS private key file.

.SS Certificate Pool Options

.TP
.B \-\-certificate \fINAME:CERT:KEY\fR
Define a named certificate for the certificate pool. Can be repeated. Example: \fB\-\-certificate "myapp:/path/to/cert.pem:/path/to/key.pem"\fR.

.SS VTTY Options

.TP
.B \-\-vtty\-rows \fIN\fR
Virtual terminal height in rows (default: \fB24\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-vtty\-cols \fIN\fR
Virtual terminal width in columns (default: \fB80\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-term \fITERM\fR
TERM value reported to child processes (default: \fBxterm-256color\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-scrollback \fIN\fR
VTTY scrollback buffer size in number of lines (default: \fB5000\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-truecolor
Enable 24-bit truecolor (16.7 million colors) in the virtual terminal.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-truecolor
Disable 24-bit truecolor.

.TP
.B \-\-mouse
Enable mouse event forwarding to child processes.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Disable mouse event forwarding.

.SS Display Options

.TP
.B \-\-display
Show VTTY output on the local terminal screen.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-display
Disable local terminal display (default).

.TP
.B \-\-display\-all
Keep displaying VTTY output after the initial CLI command exits, switching to the next available command (monitor mode). Without this flag, the display is dismissed when the CLI command finishes but the server continues running. Note: when all commands have exited (no retained commands remain), vrunner exits even in display-all mode.

.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-ms \fIMS\fR
VTTY display refresh interval in milliseconds (default: \fB100\fR).

.SS Logging Options

.TP
.B \-\-log
Log API commands to the terminal.

.TP
.B \-\-log\-file \fIFILE\fR
Log API commands to a file (also enables logging).

.SS Daemon Options

.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run as a background daemon (Unix only). Performs a double-fork to detach from the controlling terminal. Implicitly disables local display.

.TP
.B \-\-stdout\-file \fIFILE\fR
Redirect daemon stdout to this file (default: \fB/tmp/vrunner.out\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-stderr\-file \fIFILE\fR
Redirect daemon stderr to this file (default: \fB/tmp/vrunner.err\fR).

.SS Exit Handler Options

.TP
.B \-\-on\-exit \fICMD\fR
Run \fICMD\fR when a child process exits cleanly (exit code 0). The command string is split on whitespace into a binary and arguments. The handler runs as a detached (fire-and-forget) process.

.TP
.B \-\-on\-error \fICMD\fR
Run \fICMD\fR when a child process exits with a non-zero exit code. Same parsing rules as \fB\-\-on\-exit\fR. Useful for sending failure notifications or triggering cleanup/rollback scripts.

.TP
.B \-\-exit\-timeout \fISECS\fR
Maximum seconds to wait for a child process to exit after SIGINT before sending SIGKILL (default: \fB10\fR). Applies when \fBPOST /api/commands/:id/kill\fR is called or when the server shuts down. This two-phase approach prevents data corruption in processes that need to flush buffers or close connections.

.TP
.B \-\-retain\-on\-exit
Keep the VTTY buffer in memory after the child process exits. This is a \fBper\-command\fR option \[em] it only affects the command specified on the CLI, not future commands spawned via the API. The command remains visible in the tab bar and web UI with an "exited" status, allowing inspection of final output. The buffer can be manually purged via the API (DELETE /api/commands/:id) or the \fBpurge\fR subcommand. When all commands have exited and none are retained, vrunner exits even in \fB\-\-display\-all\fR mode.

.TP
.B \-\-snapshot\-on\-exit \fIFILE\fR
Save the VTTY buffer to \fIFILE\fR as plain text when the command exits. This is a per-command option. The output includes all scrollback lines followed by the visible screen rows, with each line trimmed of trailing whitespace. The snapshot is taken after the process exits but before the command is removed from the manager. Useful for capturing test output, build logs, or any command's final state.

.TP
.B \-\-send\-keys \fIKEYS\fR
Send keystrokes to the command after it starts. Uses the same key notation as the API's \fBsend_keys\fR endpoint. Plain text is sent as-is; special keys use \fB<...>\fR notation: \fB<Enter>\fR, \fB<Tab>\fR, \fB<Esc>\fR, \fB<Up>\fR, \fB<Down>\fR, \fB<Left>\fR, \fB<Right>\fR, \fB<F1>\fR through \fB<F12>\fR, \fB<C\-c>\fR (Ctrl+C), \fB<C\-d>\fR (Ctrl+D), \fB<A\-x>\fR (Alt+x). Example: \fB\-\-send\-keys "ls<Enter>"\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-snapshot\-on\-exit \fIFILE\fR
Save the VTTY buffer to a file as plain text when the command exits. The output includes scrollback content followed by the visible screen rows, with each line trimmed of trailing whitespace. The snapshot is taken after the process exits but before the command is removed from the manager. This is a per-command option.

.TP
.B \-\-send\-keys \fIKEYS\fR
Send keystrokes to the command after it starts. Uses the same key notation as the API's send_keys endpoint. Plain text is sent as-is; special keys use <...> notation: <Enter>, <Tab>, <Esc>, <Up>, <Down>, <Left>, <Right>, <F1>\-<F12>, <C\-c>, <C\-d>, <A\-x> (Alt+x). Example: \fB\-\-send\-keys "ls<Enter>\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-log\-pty\-raw \fIFILE\fR
Log raw PTY output from child processes to a file. Each line records one read() call with an elapsed-time stamp and escaped bytes (printable ASCII as-is, non-printable as \fB\\xHH\fR). The resulting log can be replayed step-by-step with \fBansi-replay\fR.

.SS Interactive Options

.TP
.B \-\-tabs
Show a tab bar listing all running commands at the top of the interactive display (requires \fB\-\-display\fR). When disabled (default), only the active command is shown. This provides an \fBmprocs\fR-style multi-command view.

.SS Environment Variable Options

.TP
.B \-\-env \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Set environment variable for spawned commands (repeatable). Overrides config file environment variables.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-env
Ignore environment variables from the config file. Only variables set via \fB\-\-env\fR flags or the API \fBenv\fR field will be passed to the spawned command.

.SS Profile Options

.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
Apply a named configuration profile from the config file. Profile fields override the base config; CLI flags override both.

.TP
.B \-\-target \fIPID\fR
Target a specific vrunner instance by PID when using spawn, freeze, thaw, or resize subcommands.

.SS Command Specification

.TP
.B \-\-
Separator that distinguishes vrunner's own flags from the child command. Everything after \fB\-\-\fR is passed as the command and its arguments. Required when the child command has flags that might conflict with vrunner's own flags.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS

.SS list
List all running vrunner instances on the system. Displays PID, port, bind address, daemon status, display status, and current command for each instance.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner list
.RE
.RE

.SS stop
Gracefully shut down a vrunner instance by its PID. Sends an HTTP shutdown request to the instance. If the instance is unresponsive, use \fBkill(1)\fR as a fallback.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner stop \fIPID\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS cert generate
Generate a new named certificate in the certificate pool. The certificate is a self-signed X.509 certificate with a derived bearer token (SHA-256 of the certificate PEM).

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner cert generate \fINAME\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS cert list
List all certificates in the pool, showing name, certificate file path, key file path, and the first 16 characters of the derived token.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner cert list
.RE
.RE

.SS cert show
Display full details of a specific certificate, including the complete 64-character bearer token.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner cert show \fINAME\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS cert remove
Remove a certificate from the pool registry. Note that this does not delete the PEM files from disk.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner cert remove \fINAME\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS spawn
Spawn a new command in a vrunner instance. Connects to a running vrunner server and requests command creation via the HTTP API. Supports all command options including terminal dimensions, environment variables, exit handlers, and certificate binding.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner spawn [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.RE
.PP
.B Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-rows \fIN\fR, \-\-cols \fIN\fR
Set the virtual terminal dimensions for the spawned command.
.TP
.BR \-\-env \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Set environment variable (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env
Ignore config file environment variables.
.TP
.BR \-\-target \fIPID\fR
Target a specific vrunner instance by PID.
.RE
.RE

.SS freeze
Freeze (SIGSTOP) a running command by its process ID. The command is paused but not terminated; use \fBthaw\fR to resume.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner freeze \fIPID\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS thaw
Thaw (SIGCONT) a previously frozen command by its process ID, resuming its execution.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner thaw \fIPID\fR
.RE
.RE

.SS list-vrunner
List all running vrunner instances on the system. Displays PID, port, bind address, daemon status, display status, and current command for each instance.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner list-vrunner
.RE
.RE

.SS list-commands
List all commands running in the target vrunner instance.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner list-commands
.RE
.RE

.SS config-check
Validate configuration files without starting the server. Reports validation errors and warnings with field paths. Checks all config sources (global, local, explicit) and reports type mismatches, unknown fields, and deprecation warnings.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner config-check
.RE
.RE

.SS purge
Purge a retained (exited) command from the manager. Permanently discards the VTTY buffer and all associated state.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner purge [\fITARGET\fR]
.RE
.PP
If no target is given and exactly one exited command exists, it is purged automatically. If the target is numeric, it is treated as a command ID (first 8 chars). Otherwise it is matched against command names.
.RE

.SS stop-command
Stop a running command in a vrunner instance. If no target is given and exactly one command is running, it is stopped automatically. If the target is numeric, it is treated as a PID. Otherwise it is matched against command names (and optionally args).

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner stop-command [\fITARGET\fR]
.RE
.RE

.SS resize
Resize a command's virtual terminal. When used without explicit \fB\-\-rows\fR or \fB\-\-cols\fR flags, the terminal is automatically resized to match the dimensions of the current terminal (auto-detect mode). When one dimension is specified, the other is auto-detected from the current terminal.

.RS
.PP
.B Usage:
.RS
vrunner resize \fITARGET\fR [\fB\-\-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-cols\fR \fIN\fR]
.RE
.RE

.SH WEB ADMIN INTERFACE

The built-in web admin dashboard is available at \fB/admin\fR on the running instance. Open a browser and navigate to:

.PP
.RS
\fBhttp://localhost:8080/admin\fR (HTTP mode)
.br
\fBhttps://localhost:8080/admin\fR (TLS mode)
.RE

.PP
The admin interface provides:
.IP \(bu 4
A list of all running commands with their status, arguments, and certificate bindings
.IP \(bu 4
A VTTY viewer that renders terminal output in the browser using the incremental diff WebSocket protocol
.IP \(bu 4
A Pause/Run button to freeze (SIGSTOP) and thaw (SIGCONT) the selected command
.IP \(bu 4
Controls for spawning new commands, sending keystrokes, and killing commands
.IP \(bu 4
Auto-selection of the first available command on load
.IP \(bu 4
1-second HTTP polling fallback when WebSocket is unavailable
.IP \(bu 4
A log viewer with search and pagination
.RE

.SH HTTP API

The REST API is the primary interface for programmatic control. All responses use a standard JSON envelope with \fBstatus\fR, \fBdata\fR, and \fBerror\fR fields.

.SS Endpoints

.TP
.B GET /api/commands
List all running commands. Returns an array of objects with \fBid\fR, \fBname\fR, \fBpid\fR, \fBstatus\fR, and \fBcertificate\fR fields.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands
Start a new command. Request body: \fB{"cmd": "string", "args": ["string"], "rows": N, "cols": N, "on_exit": "string", "on_error": "string", "exit_timeout": N, "retain_on_exit": bool, "snapshot_on_exit": "string|null", "env": {"KEY": "VALUE"}, "no_env": bool, "certificate": "string|null"}\fR. All fields except \fBcmd\fR are optional. Returns the command ID.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/keys
Send keystrokes to a running command. Request body: \fB{"keys": "string"}\fR. Supports ANSI escape sequences for special keys.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/kill
Kill a running command. Request body: \fB{"signal": "string"}\fR (optional, defaults to SIGTERM).

.TP
.B GET /api/commands/:id/vtty
Get full VTTY contents as raw ANSI text.

.TP
.B GET /api/commands/:id/vtty/html
Get VTTY contents as rendered HTML, including cursor position, terminal dimensions, and scrollback line count.

.TP
.B GET /api/commands/:id/vtty/partial?offset=N&limit=N
Get paginated VTTY content. Default offset is 0, default limit is 50.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/resize
Resize a command's virtual terminal. Request body: \fB{"rows": N, "cols": N}\fR. Valid ranges: rows 1-200, cols 1-500.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/freeze
Freeze (SIGSTOP) a running command, pausing its execution without terminating it.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/thaw
Thaw (SIGCONT) a previously frozen command, resuming its execution.

.TP
.B GET /api/commands/:id/handles
List output handles attached to a command.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/handles
Add an output handle to a command.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/kill-pid/:pid
Kill a running command by its OS process ID (as opposed to command UUID).

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/snapshot
Store a named snapshot of the command's VTTY buffer. Body: \fB{"name": "snapshot-name"}\fR. Returns snapshot metadata including timestamp and runtime.

.TP
.B GET /api/commands/:id/snapshots
List all stored snapshots for a command.

.TP
.B POST /api/commands/:id/diff
Compute a cell-level diff of the current buffer against a stored snapshot. Body: \fB{"name": "snapshot-name"}\fR. Returns the list of changed cells.

.TP
.B DELETE /api/commands/:id/snapshots/:name
Delete a stored snapshot.

.TP
.B GET /api/certificates
List all certificates in the pool with their names, file paths, and token previews.

.TP
.B GET /api/info
Get instance information including command count, certificate count, and auth status.

.TP
.B GET /api/log?search=string&offset=N&limit=N
Get command log entries with optional search filter and pagination.

.TP
.B POST /api/shutdown
Gracefully shut down the vrunner instance.

.SS Authentication

When authentication is enabled (via \fB\-\-auth\fR, \fB\-\-remote\fR, or config), include a bearer token in every API request:

.PP
.RS
\fBAuthorization: Bearer <token>\fR
.RE

.PP
The token is stored in \fB~/.config/vrunner/token\fR by default.

.SH CONFIGURATION

vrunner reads configuration from multiple sources in order of increasing precedence:

.PP
.RS
1. Built-in defaults
.br
2. Global config: \fB~/.config/vrunner/config.yaml\fR (or \fB.toml\fR/\fB.json\fR)
.br
3. Local config: \fB./vrunner.yaml\fR (or \fB.toml\fR/\fB.json\fR)
.br
4. Explicit config: any path via \fB\-c <FILE>\fR
.br
5. CLI flags (highest precedence)
.RE

.PP
The configuration file format is detected from the file extension: \fB.yaml\fR/\fB.yml\fR for YAML, \fB.toml\fR for TOML, \fB.json\fR for JSON. All three formats are fully supported with identical schemas.

.SS Configuration Sections

.TP
.B server
Controls HTTP server binding (\fBbind\fR, \fBport\fR).

.TP
.B security
Controls authentication (\fBrequire_auth\fR, \fBtoken_file\fR) and CORS (\fBcors.policy\fR).

.RS
.PP
The \fBcors\fR sub-section configures Cross-Origin Resource Sharing:
.PP
.RS
\fBpolicy\fR \fI\("any" | "none" | ORIGINS\)\fR
.br
Controls which origins are allowed for cross-origin requests. \fB"any"\fR allows all origins (default, backward compatible). \fB"none"\fR blocks all cross-origin requests. ORIGINS is a comma-separated list of allowed origins, e.g. \fB"https://myapp.example.com,https://admin.example.com"\fR.
.RE
.RE

.TP
.B tls
Controls TLS encryption (\fBenabled\fR, \fBcert_file\fR, \fBkey_file\fR).

.TP
.B certificates
Manages named certificates for per-command access control (\fBdirectory\fR, \fBentries\fR).

.TP
.B vtty
Controls virtual terminal properties (\fBrows\fR, \fBcols\fR, \fBterm\fR, \fBscrollback\fR, \fBtruecolor\fR, \fBmouse\fR).

.TP
.B display
Controls local terminal display (\fBenabled\fR, \fBrefresh_ms\fR).

.TP
.B command_log
Controls command logging (\fBenabled\fR, \fBfile\fR).

.TP
.B daemon
Controls daemon mode (\fBenabled\fR, \fBstdout_file\fR, \fBstderr_file\fR).

.TP
.B environment
Defines environment variables for spawned commands. A mapping of key-value pairs that are set in the child process environment. Can be overridden per-command via \fB\-\-env\fR flags or the API \fBenv\fR field, or suppressed entirely with \fB\-\-no\-env\fR.

.TP
.B profiles
Named configuration profiles that override base config fields. Each profile can specify any config section, and its values take precedence over the base configuration. CLI flags override profile values. A profile is selected with \fB\-\-profile <NAME>\fR.

.TP
.B handles
Defines additional output sinks for spawned commands.

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic usage

.PP
Start vrunner in idle mode (no command, waits for API requests):
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Run a command with local terminal display:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner \-\-display \-\- htop\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Run a command as a background daemon:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner \-\-daemon \-\- python \-m http.server 8000\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Run on a custom port:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner \-\-port 9090 \-\- npm run dev\fR
.fi
.RE

.SS Remote access with TLS

.PP
Start a secure remote-accessible instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner \-\-remote \-\-tls \-\- some-server\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Connect from a remote machine with curl:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl \-\-cacert ~/.config/vrunner/cert.pem \e\fR
     \fB\-H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \e\fR
     \fBhttps://server:8080/api/commands\fR
.fi
.RE

.SS Using the API

.PP
Spawn a command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl \-s \-X POST http://localhost:8080/api/commands \e\fR
     \fB\-H "Content-Type: application/json" \e\fR
     \fB\-d '{"cmd": "htop", "args": []}'\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
List running commands:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl http://localhost:8080/api/commands\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Send keystrokes to a command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl \-s \-X POST http://localhost:8080/api/commands/<id>/keys \e\fR
     \fB\-H "Content-Type: application/json" \e\fR
     \fB\-d '{"keys": "q"}'\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
View VTTY output:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl http://localhost:8080/api/commands/<id>/vtty/html\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Kill a command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl \-s \-X POST http://localhost:8080/api/commands/<id>/kill \e\fR
     \fB\-H "Content-Type: application/json" \-d '{}'\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Search command logs:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl "http://localhost:8080/api/log?search=spawn&limit=50"\fR
.fi
.RE

.SS Instance management

.PP
List all running instances:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner list\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Stop an instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner stop 12345\fR
.fi
.RE

.SS Certificate management

.PP
Generate a certificate:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner cert generate my-app\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
List certificates:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrunner cert list\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn a command bound to a certificate:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ curl \-s \-X POST http://localhost:8080/api/commands \e\fR
     \fB\-H "Content-Type: application/json" \e\fR
     \fB\-d '{"cmd": "node", "args": ["server.js"], "certificate": "my-app"}'\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH FILES

.TP
.B ~/.config/vrunner/config.yaml
Global configuration file (also \fBconfig.toml\fR or \fBconfig.json\fR).

.TP
.B ~/.config/vrunner/token
Default bearer token for API authentication.

.TP
.B ~/.config/vrunner/cert.pem
Auto-generated TLS certificate.

.TP
.B ~/.config/vrunner/key.pem
Auto-generated TLS private key.

.TP
.B ~/.config/vrunner/certs/
Default directory for certificate pool entries.

.TP
.B ./vrunner.yaml
Local configuration file (also \fBvrunner.toml\fR or \fBvrunner.json\fR).

.TP
.B /tmp/vrunner.out
Default daemon stdout redirect.

.TP
.B /tmp/vrunner.err
Default daemon stderr redirect.

.SH ENVIRONMENT

No environment variables are required. The following are recognized by child processes spawned by vrunner:

.TP
.B TERM
Set to the value of the \fB\-\-term\fR option (default: \fBxterm-256color\fR).

.TP
.B LINES
Set to the VTTY row count from \fB\-\-vtty\-rows\fR (default: \fB24\fR).

.TP
.B COLUMNS
Set to the VTTY column count from \fB\-\-vtty\-cols\fR (default: \fB80\fR).

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Successful execution or graceful shutdown.

.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid arguments, configuration error, etc.).

.TP
.B 2
Child command exited with a non-zero status (when running a command directly).

